# SYNOPSIS

```text
protocol vectraos.i2c.Bus version 1
call transfer(address: UInt16, write: [UInt8], read: UInt32)
  throws(I2CError) -> [UInt8]
```

# DESCRIPTION

Protocol `vectraos.i2c.Bus`, version 1, of library `I2CBusIPC`, its messages in the one wire format (wire(6)).

| Method | Kind | Since | Ordinal |
| `transfer` | call | 1 | `0x207dd34f0ff8c1d3` |

: `transfer`
  `write` sent to the 7-bit `address`, then, after a repeated start,
  `read` bytes read from it (a write alone, a read alone, or an
  address alone, a probe, where the other is empty): what was read.

